                    title: 'What Is International SEO? (vs. Local SEO)',
                    content: 'Quick Answer: What Is International SEO?\nInternational SEO is the practice of optimizing a website so search engines can identify and correctly serve the right language and/or country-specific version of your content to users in different regions. It differs fundamentally from [local SEO](/services/local-seo), which optimizes visibility within a single geographic area, and from simple translation, which changes text without addressing routing signals.\n\nKey Distinctions:\n• Local SEO focuses on Google Business Profiles, localized citations, and physical proximity to rank within a city or metro area.\n• International SEO focuses on URL routing, hreflang clusters, canonical parity, and multi-region crawling to rank correctly across sovereign nations and language groups.',
